{
  "id": "ss.char.tri",
  "name": "Tri",
  "description": "The sprinter, sealed like the rest and built to cut the air. The helmet carries a long crest that sweeps back to a point — the wedge it used to be — and both dead feelers lie flat along it; fins stand off the calves and the forearms; the torso is the narrowest of the eight on the thinnest limbs. What Tri does is spit, and the suit is built around it: a valved nozzle stands off the front of the helmet where a mouth would be, fed by a throat canister under the jaw and a bile line that runs down to a reservoir slung on the far hip — the one organ on any survivor still doing its job, plumbed through the suit. Teal piping on the chest and the crest, a teal line in the visor, everything else the same dark slate. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
